  "notes": "The metal-facing branch of the lane, authored as a scene preset rather than a person: an 808 kit playing against metal signifiers. Three things separate it from its parent. (1) The harmony is written as power-chord roots — root and 5th, not triads — so `extensions.triad` is near-total, `voicing.style` is open and `voicing.register` sits an octave below the parent's: drop tuning is the reason the whole model is low. (2) `melody.register` is guitar range, not bell range, because the riff *is* the hook and there is no pad above it. (3) `dissonanceBudget` is authored rather than inherited: the research names the tritone and b2 specifically as horror colour, which is a different device from the parent's half-step melodic clash. `percs.lanes` carries the crash / reversed-cymbal marker the research puts at every 8 bars. ⚠ `medium` because the research rates this high-medium and marks the tempo distribution `[LOW-CONF]` — the 130–165 range is the inferred parameter; everything else here traces to a stated trait. ⚠ The breakdown the research describes (drums out, voice and guitar only) is carried by `arrangement.sectionRules.bridge`, since the engine has no breakdown section name. ⚠ The 32nd/triplet hat bursts the research names as section markers are carried by `hihat.fillDensity`; the roll vocabulary is held to 16ths at one position so this batch's fills stay distinguishable from each other. ⚠ An authored `chords.dissonanceBudget` was removed: no generator reads it, so it was a knob that looked like a parameter and did nothing.",
